  "text": "Remote Telephone Consultations - Southfields\nPet Owners\nWhat to Expect\nOur Services\nOur Facilities\nNew Hospital\nFinance and Insurance\nPrescription Order Form\nRemote Consultations\nHearing Clinic\nBlood Donors\nFAQs\nPet Owner Events\nVet Professionals\nHow to Refer\nOur Services\nCPD Events\nMembers Area\nBlood Bank\nNew Hospital\nFixed Price Packages\nServices\nAnaesthesia and Analgesia\nCardiology and Interventional Cardiology\nClient Care\nDermatology\nDiagnostic Imaging\nExotic Pets\nInternal Medicine\nNeurology and Neurosurgery\nNursing\nOncology and Radiotherapy Suite\nOncology\nOphthalmology\nOrthopaedics\nRadiotherapy\nSoft Tissue Surgery\nTeam\nAnaesthesia and Analgesia\nCardiology and Interventional Cardiology\nCat Friendly Team\nCentral Support\nClient Care\nDermatology\nDiagnostic Imaging\nExotic Pets\nClient Finance Team\nGreen Group Team\nInternal Medicine\nNeurology and Neurosurgery\nNurses\nOncology Team\nOphthalmology Team\nOrthopaedics Team\nPatient Care Assistants\nRadiotherapy Team\nRotating Interns\nSoft Tissue Surgery\nJoin Our Team\nLeadership\nVeterinary Specialists\nNursing\nPatient Care Assistants\nAdministration Team\nInternships\nPlacements\nResidency\nSupport Team\nReferral Nursing\nPost Registration Programme\nContact\nInsight\nLatest News\nVideos\nBlog Posts\nFact Sheets\nCase Studies\nOur Pet Stories\n+44 (0)1268 564664\nVetHub\nLog in\nSign Up\n+44 (0)1268 564664\nVetHub\nLog in\nSign Up\nUPDATE: Please be aware that our opening hours have changed on Monday 19th September. Please contact us for any emergency care.\nRemote\nTelephone Consultations\nVeterinary consultations from the comfort of your own home\nSouthfields is pleased to offer remote telephone consultations for referral appointments with our Neurology, Internal Medicine, Medical Oncology and Surgery teams. Our remote consultation service enables our teams to assist clients when we are not able to provide face-to-face consultations.\nDuring a remote telephone consultation, our clinicians can:\nReview clinical history supplied by the referring vet\nProvide interpretations of diagnostics\nDiscuss your case, make recommendations and provide estimates.\nFollowing the remote consultation, an in-person follow-on consultation would be required prior to admittance, procedures, treatments, medications or prescriptions.\nBenefits of a remote telephone consultation:\nConsultations from the comfort of your own home\nAppointments lasting up to 45 minutes\nA calmer experience for anxious pets\nLimits the need for travel.\nRoyal College of Veterinary Surgeons (RCVS) Guidance\nVets work under professional guidance from the RCVS and the Medicines Act; this restricts what can be carried out remotely to diagnose and treat your pet when they are unwell.\nTo find out more or book a remote consultation contact our team on\n01268 564664\n.\nRemote Telephone Consultation Service Terms and Conditions\nDepending on the individual circumstance of any request – the final decision to conduct a remote consultation will be made by the Hospital.\nThe Remote Telephone Consultation Service can only be booked once our expert team agree it is appropriate to do so. In the first instance you must call the Hospital, where the options available will be discussed with you. Any agreed remote consultation must be pre-booked and is subject to availability.\nFees will be discussed at the time of enquiry. Payment will be taken prior to the remote consultation appointment with receipts sent via email or post. Payment for further consultations, treatments or medication will be taken as necessary at that time.\nAdvice and recommendations are made based upon the clinical history from the referring vet and information obtained from the owner at the time of the remote consultation.\nThe Hospital cannot take responsibility for the quality or interpretation of physical examinations, imaging, etc. received from external sources or provided by the owner.\nA chargeable in-person follow-on appointment (including a clinical examination) will be required to confirm the patient’s individual treatment plan ahead of admittance to the Hospital, commencement of any procedures or treatments, or prescription of any medication.\nUse of this Remote Telephone Consultation Service will be subject to our\nprivacy policy\n.\nIn addition, our\nstandard terms and conditions\nwill apply.\nAnaesthesia and Analgesia\n|\nCardiology and Interventional Cardiology\n|\nDermatology\nDiagnostic Imaging\n|\nExotics\n|\nInternal Medicine\n|\nNeurology and Neurosurgery\n|\nNursing\nOncology\n|\nOphthalmology\n|\nOrthopaedics\n|\nRadiotherapy\n|\nSoft Tissue Surgery\n|\nClient Care\nAbout Us\n|\nNew Hospital\n|\nBlog\n|\nNews\n|\nCase Studies\n|\nVideos\n|\nSustainability\nTerms of Service\n|\nLegal Notice\n|\nModern Slavery Act\n|\nCookies Policy\n|\nPrivacy Statement\n|\nAccessibility\nGender Pay Gap Report\n|\nCustomer Charter\n|\nComplaints\nCookies Settings\nLinnaeus Veterinary Limited (trading as): Southfields Veterinary Specialists\nPart of Linnaeus, an Affiliate of Mars, Incorporated\nCranes Point\n|\nGardiners Lane South\n|\nBasildon\n|\nEssex\n|\nSS14 3AP\n|\nT +44 (0)1268 564664\nRegistered address: Friars Gate 1011 Stratford Road Solihull B90 4BN\nRegistered in England & Wales Company no. 10790375  |  VAT Reg 195 0928 77\nCopyright © 2026 Southfields Veterinary Specialists |\nHosting and Maintenance by Clickingmad",
